RSAM Event algorithm:  I'm a little hazy on the details, but it is akin to =
an STA/LTA but instead uses maybe 5-second RSAM values for the "average". I=
f the RSAM values being collected every 5.12? seconds are of a series R(1),=
 R(2), R(3), R(4) etc it compares not the current value not to the immediat=
ely preceding value, but the value before that (comparing R(4) with R(2) fo=
r instance).  This is done because if an event arrived sometime in the R(3)=
 time period it would have an unknown mix of pre-event and event data. R(2)=
 would be the clean pre-event arrival average and R(4) the post event arriv=
al average.



And there are no cross-station comparison.  It is designed to be run on a s=
ingle station, like one doing event counts from a paper seismiogram.



