<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Aptos, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;f=
ont-size:12pt;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">
Below is the directory tree I put together from re-organizing files that yo=
u, Randy, and JP gave me. The whole archive is only 12 GB currently, as an =
Earthscope Assembled Dataset. It=E2=80=99s =E2=80=9Crestricted=E2=80=9D cur=
rently, as I=E2=80=99m working with JP to get permission from PHIVOLCS
 to make the data open.</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Aptos, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;f=
ont-size:12pt;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">
<br clear=3D"none">
</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Aptos, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;f=
ont-size:12pt;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">
The LEGACY folder is the original data formats. FAIR is converted - just wa=
veforms converted to MiniSEED so far, but I did convert phase picks and hyp=
ocenters to QuakeML too. I plan to convert RSAM to MiniSEED: I think channe=
l UHZ is correct for 60-s data,
 and RHZ for 600-s data. SSAM might be best as HDF5. Irregular time series =
just as timestamped rows in CSV?</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Aptos, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;f=
ont-size:12pt;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">
<br clear=3D"none">
</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Aptos, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;f=
ont-size:12pt;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">
<b>I wonder if you=E2=80=99d be willing to have a phone call? </b>I=E2=80=
=99d really like to pick your brain about the development of the VDAP Mobil=
e Monitoring System, and components like RSAM, BOB, XDETECT/MDETECT etc., a=
nd what relationship they have to the IASPEI tools
 by Willie Lee and others. And I wonder if you have the source code for any=
 of those - and Glowworm?&nbsp;</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Aptos, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;f=
ont-size:12pt;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">
<br clear=3D"none">
</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Aptos, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;f=
ont-size:12pt;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">
Incidentally, I just had a call with Robert Banfill, who co-authored some o=
f the SUDS library. We=E2=80=99re going to work on a direct Linux/Mac multi=
plexed SUDS to MiniSEED converter with IRIG-E time correction. I wonder abo=
ut converting/replicating some of your codes
 too, and publishing them in the Journal of Open Source Software - I could =
do the work, if you are willing to guide. Just a thought.</div>
