I just checked Fire and Mud. The Pinatubo RSAM was still the Model 100 vers=
ion.&nbsp; From the USGS openb-file report on the Model 100 version&nbsp;</=
div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-siz=
e:16px;" class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydp23bce3=
03yiv3947432043ydp994f9837yahoo-style-wrap">
<br clear=3D"none">
</div>
</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin-right:0px;margin-left:40px;font-family:Hel=
vetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:16px;" class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv094012288=
6ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydp23bce303yiv3947432043ydp994f9837yahoo-style-wra=
p">
&quot;At the beginning of each minute, a call to the data-acquisition sub-p=
rogram causes the Model 100/102 to digitize 125 samples for each seismic in=
put at a rate of about 50 samples/second/input and return the sums of the d=
igitized values.&quot;</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-siz=
e:16px;" class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydp23bce3=
03yiv3947432043ydp994f9837yahoo-style-wrap">
<br clear=3D"none">
</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-siz=
e:16px;" class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydp23bce3=
03yiv3947432043ydp994f9837yahoo-style-wrap">
So the event data would have been the RSAM average taken over about 2.5 sec=
onds (125 samples/(50 samples/second)). I think you understand that everyth=
ing is approximate because of the limitations of the Model 100. You couldn'=
t sample the data in background
 like I was able to when I converted to the PC-based RSAM.&nbsp; I recall t=
hat I got to 50 samples/second/input by just experiementing with a simple l=
oop interation delay between taking a sample until it seemed to be close to=
 the desired 50 sps /input channel.</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-siz=
e:16px;" class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydp23bce3=
03yiv3947432043ydp994f9837yahoo-style-wrap">
<br clear=3D"none">
</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-siz=
e:16px;" class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydp23bce3=
03yiv3947432043ydp994f9837yahoo-style-wrap">
So the Model 100 would grab 125 samples, halt digitizing for a bit to proce=
ss the data and then go back for another 125 samples. The RSAM openfile est=
imates that over a minute less than 15% of the time (~9 seconds/minute) was=
 devoted to processing and transferring
 the data for BOB storage. Not sampling during that 9 seconds was another r=
eason for the classical earthquake seismologists to initially dismiss RSAM.=
&nbsp; &nbsp;</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-siz=
e:16px;" class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydp23bce3=
03yiv3947432043ydp994f9837yahoo-style-wrap">
<br clear=3D"none">
</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-siz=
e:16px;" class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydp23bce3=
03yiv3947432043ydp994f9837yahoo-style-wrap">
When I went to the PC-based RSAM I think I went to 100 samples/second, but =
would have to double-check that.</div>
<div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-siz=
e:16px;" class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydp23bce3=
