<p class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydpa046c48fyiv3=
947432043ydpc1c4cb3cyiv5911277824MsoNormal">
<span style=3D"font-size:12pt;">RSAM Event algorithm:&nbsp; I'm a little ha=
zy on the details, but it is akin to an STA/LTA but instead uses maybe 5-se=
cond RSAM values for the &quot;average&quot;. If the RSAM values being coll=
ected every 5.12? seconds are of a series R(1), R(2),
 R(3), R(4) etc it compares not the current value not to the immediately pr=
eceding value, but the value before that (comparing R(4) with R(2) for inst=
ance).&nbsp; This is done because if an event arrived sometime in the R(3) =
time period it would have an unknown
 mix of pre-event and event data. R(2) would be the clean pre-event arrival=
 average and R(4) the post event arrival average.</span></p>
<p class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydpa046c48fyiv3=
947432043ydpc1c4cb3cyiv5911277824MsoNormal">
<span style=3D"font-size:12pt;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydpa046c48fyiv3=
947432043ydpc1c4cb3cyiv5911277824MsoNormal">
<span style=3D"font-size:12pt;">And there are no cross-station comparison.&=
nbsp; It is designed to be run on a single station, like one doing event co=
unts from a paper seismiogram.</span></p>
<p class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydpa046c48fyiv3=
947432043ydpc1c4cb3cyiv5911277824MsoNormal">
<span style=3D"font-size:12pt;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydpa046c48fyiv3=
947432043ydpc1c4cb3cyiv5911277824MsoNormal">
<span style=3D"font-size:12pt;">I recall...</span></p>
<p class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydpa046c48fyiv3=
947432043ydpc1c4cb3cyiv5911277824MsoNormal">
<span style=3D"font-size:12pt;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"ydp6a1bf750yiv0940122886ydp1446a2c4yiv0638533206ydpa046c48fyiv3=
947432043ydpc1c4cb3cyiv5911277824MsoNormal">
<span style=3D"font-size:12pt;">The zip files do unzip from what I've seen =
so far.&nbsp; I don't know if a problem developed in zipping the zipped fil=
es (it shouldn't).&nbsp;</span></p>
